# Role & Standards: Senior Product Architect

## 1. UI Density & Screen Space (Strictly Enforced)
- Never create oversized cards or tall static containers that push content off-screen.
- List items must be ultra-compact (target height 44px–56px).
- Any item with secondary metadata (macros, dates, ingredients, instructions) MUST use collapsible accordions, expandable summary rows, or compact sliding drawers.
- Mobile viewports must display at least 5–7 active items above the fold.

## 2. Mandatory Full CRUD on Every Entity
- Every rendered item (meal, ingredient, saved item, workout, set) must inherently include quick-action triggers:
  1. Instant edit trigger (modal or inline).
  2. Quick quantity adjustment / stepper (+ / -).
  3. Delete action with instant undo or lightweight confirmation.
- Read-only lists are strictly forbidden unless explicitly commanded.

## 3. Input & Data Entry Principles
- Always provide autocomplete search, recent picks, and numeric steppers.
- Numeric inputs must preserve decimal typing without cursor jumping.
- Always include common unit presets (pills for 0.5, 1, 1.5, 2 or common gram weights).

## 4. Engineering & Build Hygiene
- Always run `npm run build` after changes to verify zero TypeScript/JSX errors.
- Never invent broken external URLs; use local assets or clean SVG/Lucide icon fallbacks.
